  "records": [
    {
      "id": "i01",
      "section": "motivation",
      "text": "Archive metadata can make a table look ready for a mass-metallicity census in two very different ways.",
      "text_sha256": "d6c66b0e5d942eb97b078572b689a387160c00f6ce83ea8c9c2df765dc3552ee",
      "file": "audio/mzr-census/raw/i01-d6c66b0e5d94.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "6159e695e1d3605412fb352fee0443ee89fd51f7e4a909039382397d3b910a75",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "6.456000",
          "size": "103296"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "i02",
      "section": "motivation",
      "text": "If mass, gas-phase abundance, and redshift were genuinely joined within one galaxy sample, that would let us test how enrichment changes with galaxy mass across cosmic time.",
      "text_sha256": "d0eed80a46b647670669ac2d371409abcae506b0b794241db4a06ef74c7782f6",
      "file": "audio/mzr-census/raw/i02-d0eed80a46b6.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "7fab62080775bf11ff5876fa3e1231be754228b3de1b18ffec15d29a99d89e6a",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "8.544000",
          "size": "136704"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "i03",
      "section": "motivation",
      "text": "But an apparent three-axis match could instead be a fact about archive symbols and metadata, not about a galaxy sample.",
      "text_sha256": "75c28d7077efd85ccff693641d0c7816ccfb1fa076e6f923a3310ec33b004112",
      "file": "audio/mzr-census/raw/i03-75c28d7077ef.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "3d7e4f1a398668397ccc70cc882e64c5dc5d7ba7cf411a995784307580631fb5",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "7.128000",
          "size": "114048"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "i04",
      "section": "motivation",
      "text": "How do we tell a reachable table from an eligible one?",
      "text_sha256": "643839b04ce239b57a644fe1fab33aa8288765c4812594e1ce03f344e73f538e",
      "file": "audio/mzr-census/raw/i04-643839b04ce2.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "065f5dba55403997edda2fa9d1b30c16902d3ce70c373d71ff917a326575dd4b",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "3.912000",
          "size": "62592"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "d01",
      "section": "difficulty",
      "text": "Counting metadata hits cannot settle that question, because one symbol can name redshift, Galactic height, or a model-grid composition.",
      "text_sha256": "6556711709d4e39fb84568e7377294c8ef434ac2eef2ac76700f0a6f2687c590",
      "file": "audio/mzr-census/raw/d01-6556711709d4.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "b6a2dab58cac837542edbc038f142e9ef0510b4597d8ed5bbc169b7b5a1a1883",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "8.112000",
          "size": "129792"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "d02",
      "section": "difficulty",
      "text": "The census therefore needs evidence that the required quantities refer to the right physical species, phase, and parent sample in the same table.",
      "text_sha256": "8b74b49265158dd218a12795aa5ec6601de9809d63e384e490809c5f43acdbdb",
      "file": "audio/mzr-census/raw/d02-8b74b4926515.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "c20e5922044b50f4e48b6dcc1358fad7b5fef8a6e9f3d2feb3e6dba8ed9ee7f0",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "6.960000",
          "size": "111360"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "p01",
      "section": "peak",
      "text": "The discriminating move is semantic adjudication, performed on every candidate under clauses frozen before any eligibility value is computed.",
      "text_sha256": "21a6836ae181bda10132254e3bb3e659a2db53c1bba26e7edaa45cd377d3ba8a",
      "file": "audio/mzr-census/raw/p01-21a6836ae181.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "2d030906df57547a85711af25c0e358406bfa83f1e9ff2ae1dbf445e34345d67",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "8.880000",
          "size": "142080"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "p02",
      "section": "peak",
      "text": "For each required axis, the adjudicator reads the column name, the UCD qualifier, and the archived description rather than trusting the tag alone.",
      "text_sha256": "acddd1770fa3c1037b6c996d50b32a33169cde5aa6cdb347654a2b5128db2882",
      "file": "audio/mzr-census/raw/p02-acddd1770fa3.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "0b3d59095ca6ee325be558893d264634e21062ca15331d3fa959d900c47a683b",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "8.112000",
          "size": "129792"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "p03",
      "section": "peak",
      "text": "Abundance must describe an element ratio in gas, mass must be stellar mass, and redshift must identify the galaxy rather than a foreground coordinate.",
      "text_sha256": "fb66fd74abc3471f63f060b8d9dc29d74b5a08131528d956a559b728d340bbaa",
      "file": "audio/mzr-census/raw/p03-fb66fd74abc3.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "650ce7051dc24093e98f4a4d7f560aefbd388a3b531ffd66967859f67e9c82f8",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "9.048000",
          "size": "144768"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "p04",
      "section": "peak",
      "text": "Only a same-table evidence chain can support eligibility; a metadata coincidence remains on the other side of the decision boundary.",
      "text_sha256": "b990b552fba62956ea76e50e4151ec1b6973674c45fd4a3e6c490bec0fda7473",
      "file": "audio/mzr-census/raw/p04-b990b552fba6.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "09f97da87df2243fa532cce54d9bd8fb8d783bcfa8f6b86b10b00fa8ae84fee5",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "7.776000",
          "size": "124416"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "p05",
      "section": "peak",
      "text": "That decision rule is what separates a census of scientific holdings from a census of search vocabulary, while leaving the final value withheld.",
      "text_sha256": "efcb86c583345b9c437001401e86a21c184e7d7fb804f0cafee892617102fa49",
      "file": "audio/mzr-census/raw/p05-efcb86c58334.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "518ab9e8854a7951893ba38fd2682b0b5653f1a26fbb275159f509547096b530",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "7.632000",
          "size": "122112"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "f01",
      "section": "sample",
      "text": "First, record every archive table reached by mass, abundance, and redshift metadata, without treating any retrieval total as a scientific sample.",
      "text_sha256": "da87078ccd8e0bbf71af191cbdba9d9b8629b0039812b6efcaabadfef98a2074",
      "file": "audio/mzr-census/raw/f01-da87078ccd8e.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "aad080143b22b7d355ee3a290f442b198eae045dc2dd46e9ef7c7f62102d62f5",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "8.376000",
          "size": "134016"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "f02",
      "section": "sample",
      "text": "Then apply the frozen modifier filter and semantic clauses, while withholding every stage total and the final eligibility fraction.",
      "text_sha256": "6c5cc3af592537191186bce9f1bb09606ddd34bd0344e610ffccda687009cde5",
      "file": "audio/mzr-census/raw/f02-6c5cc3af5925.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "40885928fb3c03880b0d538f7010441ddfc62afc8eb8a1e381c822fa70cd2096",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "7.512000",
          "size": "120192"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "e01",
      "section": "estimator",
      "text": "The estimator is built progressively as eligible samples over adjudicated metadata candidates, with no evaluated fraction shown.",
      "text_sha256": "49f3aab3f7e374dd65615958ace0f3d7d77dfb5db58849d6d65eb45c6dde1432",
      "file": "audio/mzr-census/raw/e01-49f3aab3f7e3.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "c06287338daee6d0b07c2d689176bd4db951701ef7ff171410a9a1849eb509e1",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "6.960000",
          "size": "111360"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "e02",
      "section": "estimator",
      "text": "The denominator must be the adjudicated candidate set, because dividing by raw search hits would turn retrieval noise into a scientific rate.",
      "text_sha256": "1533df4e9f06aed1cd6fd62da6d4a2dee8ca248ab16975e1bfc565193a4ed568",
      "file": "audio/mzr-census/raw/e02-1533df4e9f06.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "3a465d57a4d2aac108982ae61578f24285f8eb96ad9948d6a833af1312174d6b",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "7.440000",
          "size": "119040"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "c01",
      "section": "controls",
      "text": "Recall controls test whether the retrieval misses known holdings, while exclusion decoys test whether metadata collisions slip through.",
      "text_sha256": "114423d48070b1672efc5984a942e74120b341dd7065f6f39ed887d797bef69f",
      "file": "audio/mzr-census/raw/c01-114423d48070.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "66f714b445b4e3c25227c7c4bbb4d97b7f515f538d9a8e2b6d5e63e441386145",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "6.672000",
          "size": "106752"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "c02",
      "section": "controls",
      "text": "Species, phase, and same-table checks are bias controls by design; this canary does not display their outcomes.",
      "text_sha256": "db361762bf404513285612ed649dad64985927dc62df9a1edb26bf8deab00315",
      "file": "audio/mzr-census/raw/c02-db361762bf40.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "4c0495dbfc21d01ff7b953107a78d6bd9b8628043f6813740024f86ba508644d",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "6.336000",
          "size": "101376"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "g01",
      "section": "discipline",
      "text": "We tied our own hands by freezing the axes, evidence clauses, exclusions, and denominator before applying the eligibility rule.",
      "text_sha256": "9f1a08015f812cd65199df2e342ec60fa05986c007c30c0ebce7e0db7455df1d",
      "file": "audio/mzr-census/raw/g01-9f1a08015f81.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "a066dfef29460db037403888a45146f764ae24b46445f0aa3ab7b463e7bd8baf",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "7.608000",
          "size": "121728"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "g02",
      "section": "discipline",
      "text": "The review gates are self-imposed scientific discipline: later convenience cannot redefine what an eligible mass-metallicity sample means.",
      "text_sha256": "a8eca9152fcacc2ef1cd826becfc9acd97e20f3f009bde765c4e13e9e9710cc5",
      "file": "audio/mzr-census/raw/g02-a8eca9152fca.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "a8396fde52dc913508b03b9fe60af00c78fc1eeb81486e9aee7d9a213103a401",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "7.824000",
          "size": "125184"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "b01",
      "section": "boundary",
      "text": "What is known is the retrieval design and source accounting; eligibility, its fraction, and any scientific interpretation remain outside this canary.",
      "text_sha256": "b56cda3fcdb07485cd51074e2d67813f7eee0e96fe7f9fe0c249d4bca31f10ce",
      "file": "audio/mzr-census/raw/b01-b56cda3fcdb0.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "7e286ab8d27265042605b6313fc7534cabd30e72ee0e3af68e48c43c52a000d4",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "8.544000",
          "size": "136704"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "x01",
      "section": "payoff",
      "text": "Ask the opening question again: are we seeing coherent galaxy tables, or only the vocabulary of the archive?",
      "text_sha256": "a4e35ac34a84a01f54a8c324a4ca1c6bcdbdc8a896d35a3c3525ea6c45c4b522",
      "file": "audio/mzr-census/raw/x01-a4e35ac34a84.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "d5c73dc88b57480089bff1b0ca4c73810546907d8ae2ffcb67971f0b882c727a",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "6.456000",
          "size": "103296"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "x02",
      "section": "payoff",
      "text": "Now we have a method that can tell those explanations apart without pretending that a result has already been authorized.",
      "text_sha256": "adae4e2e47062fa4743722069f13a9d3c325f3be46c020195e0bbb3a5821126f",
      "file": "audio/mzr-census/raw/x02-adae4e2e4706.mp3",
